# <%= it.scope %>/storage

[`@mfeflow/storage`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mfeflow/storage) under the company's scope, with nothing
added: the same `createStorage`, and `useStoredState` from `/react`. It exists so apps import every shared package
from <%= it.scope %> and never from ours, and so <%= it.scope %>/theme has something of yours to build on. It is
the place to add a company-wide helper later.

```ts
import { createStorage } from '<%= it.scope %>/storage';

const storage = createStorage('checkout');
storage.set('lastStep', 'payment');
```

## Settings only, no state

`<%= it.scope %>/storage` is not a Module Federation singleton, so every remote gets its own copy of this package.
That is fine while it only re-exports and builds things. Keep it that way: no module-level state here.
